# Pre-commit Verification

Whenever you feel you have finished editing files, run pre-commit and fix any reported issues before finishing the task:

```bash
uv run pre-commit run --all-files
```

Equivalent Makefile target: `make pc`

## When to run

- After editing Python, Vue/TS, config, or other tracked project files
- Whenever you believe the edit pass is complete — do not wait for the user to ask
- Before claiming work is complete or ready to commit

## If hooks fail

1. Fix every reported issue (lint, format, etc.) — do not leave failures for the user
2. If a formatter hook modified files, include those changes
3. Re-run `uv run pre-commit run --all-files` until all hooks pass

Do not skip hooks or stop after only running the command without fixing failures.
